codex
The handler currently writes from inside a React state updater, so React can replay the write and fast clicks can race with stale reaction state. I’m moving persistence into a per-comment queue: clicks update the optimistic view immediately, then each save runs in order; a failed save is removed and the UI is recalculated from the last confirmed state plus any later clicks.
